{
  "_readme": [
    "Source of truth for the site's photography. The image files themselves are NOT in the repository",
    "(wwwroot/img/ is gitignored) — this manifest plus scripts/fetch-media.mjs is what makes them",
    "reproducible. Run `npm run fetch:media` from ClientApp/ after a fresh clone.",
    "",
    "DEPLOYMENT: a clean CI checkout has no images. `npm run fetch:media` must run before",
    "`dotnet publish`, or wwwroot/img must be populated on the server. This is the same class of trap",
    "as the untracked appsettings.Development.json — the build will succeed and the site will render",
    "empty covers rather than failing loudly.",
    "",
    "LICENSING: Unsplash and Pexels both permit commercial use with no attribution required. Credit is",
    "recorded here anyway, because knowing where an asset came from is worth more than the licence",
    "strictly demands — and because if a photo is ever pulled, this is the only record of what it was.",
    "",
    "Resizing is done by the Unsplash CDN via the w= parameter at fetch time, which is why this needs",
    "no sharp/ImageSharp dependency. Two widths only: 800 for cards, 1600 for heroes."
  ],

  "outputRoot": "../wwwroot/img",
  "widths": [800, 1600],
  "quality": 78,

